47
00:03:52,807 --> 00:03:58,269
centavos, and the collection must remain empty. This is a test of absence of side

48
00:03:58,282 --> 00:04:02,394
effects, so a correct error message is only the beginning of the evidence you need to

49
00:04:02,407 --> 00:04:03,007
collect.

50
00:04:05,226 --> 00:04:10,201
For the idempotency case, prepare one request body and one key before sending either

51
00:04:10,214 --> 00:04:16,576
request. Reuse both values for the second submission. The fixture must belong to this

52
00:04:16,589 --> 00:04:22,264
case alone, and the two requests are sequential. In the correct local contract, the

53
00:04:22,276 --> 00:04:27,764
first response creates the transfer and the second returns the existing transfer. Two

54
00:04:27,776 --> 00:04:32,264
independent browser clicks with newly generated keys represent different intentions,

55
00:04:32,514 --> 00:04:37,388
so they would not test this rule. Inspect the request construction carefully when

56
00:04:37,401 --> 00:04:39,789
reviewing an AI-generated implementation.

57
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:47,333
Parse both responses and compare their transfer identifiers. Then perform the state

58
00:04:47,345 --> 00:04:51,770
checks: the source balance is ninety thousand centavos and there is exactly one

59
00:04:51,782 --> 00:04:57,095
transfer record with that identifier. Reload the page and verify the visible balance

60
00:04:57,108 --> 00:05:02,583
as a UI observation. Matching identifiers alone would not exclude an implementation

61
00:05:02,595 --> 00:05:08,120
that accidentally debits twice while returning the same identifier. State and identity

62
00:05:08,133 --> 00:05:13,620
therefore answer different questions. Keep both assertions, if AI suggests simplifying

63
00:05:13,633 --> 00:05:15,782
the case to make it shorter or faster.

64
00:05:17,998 --> 00:05:22,536
Run the three cases in the supplied TypeScript project and inspect the actual report.

65
00:05:23,398 --> 00:05:29,261
During diagnosis, begin without retries so the first failure remains visible. A failed

66
00:05:29,273 --> 00:05:34,348
case is useful evidence when its assertion reflects the business contract. Read the

67
00:05:34,361 --> 00:05:39,511
test name, the expected and actual values, and the associated request or trace before

68
00:05:39,523 --> 00:05:45,961
editing code. If startup failed, report a preparation failure separately. Do not label

69
00:05:45,973 --> 00:05:50,923
generated tests as passed because they compile, or because a previous execution used

70
00:05:50,936 --> 00:05:53,011
another application build and dataset.

71
00:05:55,224 --> 00:05:59,649
Give AI a focused review task: inspect these three tests for missing business

72
00:05:59,662 --> 00:06:04,949
assertions, shared mutable data, invented APIs, and waits that could hide a defect.

73
00:06:05,812 --> 00:06:11,062
Include the contract and a sanitized failure excerpt. Ask it to explain every

74
00:06:11,074 --> 00:06:16,312
suggested change and identify the evidence supporting that change. Review the patch

75
00:06:16,324 --> 00:06:21,862
before applying it. A useful suggestion may improve a locator or cleanup block; an

76
00:06:21,874 --> 00:06:26,049
unacceptable suggestion changes ninety thousand to eighty thousand merely because a

77
00:06:26,062 --> 00:06:29,599
defective implementation produced that value during an actual run.

78
00:06:31,826 --> 00:06:36,676
Your TypeScript checkpoint consists of three isolated cases, not simply three browser

79
00:06:36,689 --> 00:06:42,914
